A turn on spare time ends at a call that stopped for an interrupt,
so another thread runs before the call is made again.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call stopped where its caller cannot make it again

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -1068,7 +1068,7 @@ void sched_tick(uint32_t ticks)
  */
 static void spare_end(struct core *core)
 {
-    if (core->run_queue != 0 && !core->recall && sched_spare_turn(core)) {
+    if (core->run_queue != 0 && sched_spare_turn(core)) {
         sched_turn_end();
     }
 }
